{
  "mn118:0.1": "Middle Discourses 118 ",
  "mn118:0.2": "Mindfulness of Breathing ",
  "mn118:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn118:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery, together with several well-known senior disciples, such as ",
  "mn118:1.3": "the venerables Sāriputta, Mahāmoggallāna, Mahākassapa, Mahākaccāna, Mahākoṭṭhita, Mahākappina, Mahācunda, Anuruddha, Revata, Ānanda, and others. ",
  "mn118:2.1": "Now at that time the senior monks were advising and instructing the junior monks. ",
  "mn118:2.2": "Some senior monks instructed ten monks, while some instructed twenty, thirty, or forty. ",
  "mn118:2.3": "Being instructed by the senior monks, the junior monks realized a higher distinction than they had before. ",
  "mn118:3.1": "Now, at that time it was the sabbath—the full moon on the fifteenth day—and the Buddha was sitting surrounded by the Saṅgha of monks for the invitation to admonish. ",
  "mn118:3.2": "Then the Buddha looked around the Saṅgha of monks, who were so very silent. He addressed them: ",
  "mn118:4.1": "“I am satisfied, monks, with this practice. ",
  "mn118:4.2": "My heart is satisfied with this practice. ",
  "mn118:4.3": "So you should rouse up even more energy for attaining the unattained, achieving the unachieved, and realizing the unrealized. ",
  "mn118:4.4": "I will wait here in Sāvatthī for the Komudī full moon of the fourth month.” ",
  "mn118:5.1": "Mendican